  "note": "Triennial election of Omagh Urban District Council, January 1929. Nominations were received by Mr. W. J. Corker on Saturday 5 January 1929. No ward was contested: North Ward returned seven Unionists and West Ward seven Nationalist and Labour members unopposed, and in the South Ward the retiring member James M'Gillion, not selected at the Nationalist convention, withdrew on the Monday, so the other seven were returned unopposed (Ulster Herald, 12 January 1929, p. 5). Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Ulster Herald, 12 January 1929, p. 5 (w8-review, Nov 2026): the note said the South Ward was contested; no ward was, as M'Gillion withdrew. Hugh Friel and William F. Townsend are now Labour, as the Herald prints them (were Nationalist)."
